            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$y=\\frac{x+10}{3},\\quad x<-4$.",
              "worked": "From part b, $y=\\frac{x+10}{3}$ and $y<2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x+10}{3}&<2\\\\x+10&<6\\\\x&<-4\\end{align*}$$\nThus $y=\\frac{x+10}{3}$, with domain $x<-4$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 30
          },
          {
            "id": "p11-q10-c",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "g",
            "prompt": "For part c.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$y=\\sqrt[3]{x-2},\\quad x<29$.",
              "worked": "From part c, $y=\\sqrt[3]{x-2}$ and $y<3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt[3]{x-2}&<3\\\\x-2&<27\\\\x&<29\\end{align*}$$\nCubing preserves the inequality because the cube function is increasing.\nThus $y=\\sqrt[3]{x-2}$, with domain $x<29$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 30
          },
          {
            "id": "p11-q10-d",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "h",
            "prompt": "For part d.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$y=\\frac{13-x}{6},\\quad x\\le-5$.",
              "worked": "From part d, $y=\\frac{13-x}{6}$ and $y\\ge3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{13-x}{6}&\\ge3\\\\13-x&\\ge18\\\\-x&\\ge5\\\\x&\\le-5\\end{align*}$$\nMultiplying by $-1$ reverses the inequality.\nThus $y=\\frac{13-x}{6}$, with domain $x\\le-5$.",
